L000510	\par We simulate the group indices of the pump ($\mathrm{TE_0}$), signal ($\mathrm{TE_0}$), and idler ($\mathrm{TE_2}$) modes for waveguides with different geometric parameters. These simulated results show how waveguide geometry shapes modal dispersion and determine whether the group-velocity-matching (GVM) condition can be satisfied for all three interacting fields. Achieving GVM requires that the pump's group index lie between those of the signal and idler. The results reveal that the required group-velocity ordering can be compactly expressed as $\left(v_{g,s}^{-1}-v_{g,p}^{-1}\right)/\left(v_{g,p}^{-1}-v_{g,i}^{-1}\right) \ge 0$,
